 "text": "Hello! How was your day? Well, it really depends on the type of oil you're using. Some oils dry faster than others. So it would be best to check the can or the package for the specific drying time. No, that's not a good idea. It's better to let the oil painting dry completely. That way, you avoid any issues with the varnish. Yes, you can use a paste wax. It' a temporary option that you can remove later if needed. The best way to tell is by rubbing your finger across the surface of the painting. If it leaves an oily residue, the paint is not dry yet. If it's dry, it will feel slightly rough to the fingertips. That's the sign that the paint has fully dried.",
